  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 635 AM EST Friday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Cooler, dry, and breezy today and tomorrow. A \ncold front brings another round of rain Sunday night into Monday. \n\nStrong sfc low pressure has pulled well north of the area as of \nearly this morning. A little bit of wrap around moisture led to very \nlight scattered showers in the last several hours. While this has \nmostly come to an end, a few misty showers are certainly possible \nthis morning. Otherwise, remaining mostly cloudy and breezy today. \nSouthwest winds will be 15 to 20mph with gusts around 30mph. Cooler \ntemps today with highs in the mid 50s. High pressure slowly builds \nin from the south/southeast overnight through Sunday, leading to \ngradually clearing skies and diminishing winds. Southwest winds of \n10-15mph with gusts around 20mph Saturday, then light south winds \nSunday. Temps become milder with highs around 60 on Sat, then mid \n60s Sunday. \n\nA cold front approaches the area late Sunday and passes through \nsometime Monday morning. While it does look like this will bring \nadditional rain to the area Sunday night, QPF doesn't look \nsubstantial so far. Probs for even just half an inch are sitting in \nthe 10-30% zone in the NBM, GEFS, and Euro Ens. A brief cool down \nback to the 50s is expected behind the front, but this likely won't \nlast long given the weak UL flow depicted in guidance.  \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Moderate to major coastal flooding continues\ntoday across the upper Bay with nuisance to minor flood\nelsewhere.\n\nNow that winds have shifted to SW, tidal anomalies have begun \nto decrease across the middle and lower Ches Bay as well as the \nAtlantic coastline. However, minor coastal flooding is expected \nwith this afternoon's high tide across portions of the middle \nBay as well as the Atlantic side of the Eastern Shore. As such, \nportions of the Coastal Flood Warning have been converted into \nCoastal Flood Advisories for this afternoon's high tide. \nFarther north, moderate coastal flooding is expected across the \nbay side of the VA Eastern Shore, with major flooding expected \nat Cambridge and Bishops Head over the next two high tides. As \nsuch, Coastal Flood Warnings here remain in effect through this \nafternoon across the VA Eastern Shore and through this evening \nacross bay side of the lower MD Eastern Shore. Farther south \nacross the lower Ches Bay, Virginia Beach, and eastern \nCurrituck, additional coastal flooding is not anticipated at \nthis time outside of nuisance flooding. Conditions improve by \nSat with only nuisance flooding possible along the Eastern \nShore.\n\nIn addition to elevated water levels, dangerous surf along the \nAtlantic coast will continue to result in shoreline erosion and\nlocalized overwash. High Surf Advisories remain in effect across\nVA Beach and eastern Currituck through 10 AM and across the \nEastern Shore through 1 PM.",
